      "id": "s1",
      "text": "This block, 5 kilograms, sits on an incline tilted about 22 degrees. Start by naming the forces acting on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Gravity pulls the block straight down with mg, about 49 newtons. Split that weight into a part along the slope and a part into the surface."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "The part along the slope is mg sin θ, about 18 newtons here. That component is what pushes the block down the incline."
    }
